      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The shoreline that would become Islands Brygge was a shallow beach until the 1620s, when Christianshavn was reclaimed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islands_Brygge",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "German troops occupied Islands Brygge during WWII, and Danish resistance fighters carried out several sabotage acts there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
